Summary

The filename parameter is vulnerable to path traversal. By changing its value to ../../../etc/passwd, the application reads a file outside the intended image directory.

Steps
Intercept the request for a product image in Burp Suite.
Find the filename parameter.

Change its value to:

../../../etc/passwd
Send the request and observe the response.
Impact

An attacker could read sensitive files from the server, such as configuration files, credentials, or application data.

PoC
GET /image?filename=../../../etc/passwd HTTP/2

The response contains the contents of /etc/passwd.

Fix

Don't directly use user-controlled input as a file path. Validate the filename against an allowlist and make sure the resolved path stays inside the intended directory.
